<title>USA: King World Q2 net per share rises.</title>
<headline>King World Q2 net per share rises.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended February 28,</p>
<p>		     (in millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				  1997	1996  Change</p>
<p> Revenues		  $ 175.2   $ 176.8  (1%)</p>
<p> Net income		   36.7	35.2    4%</p>
<p> Earnings per share	 0.97	0.93    4%</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>number of shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		 37.8	37.7</p>
<p>			  Six Months Ended February 28,</p>
<p>			 (in millions except per share amounts)</p>
<p>				 1997	 1996  Change</p>
<p> Revenues		  $ 339.5   $ 338.9     -</p>
<p> Net income		   71.6     68.5*    5%</p>
<p> Earnings per share	 1.90     1.83*    4%</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>number of shares</p>
<p>  outstanding		 37.8	37.4</p>
<p>* Excludes nonrecurring gain of approximately $10.3 million or approximately $0.28 per share from the sale of Buffalo Broadcasting Co Inc to LIN Television Corporation.</p>
<p>Q2 1997 operating income rose to $50.2 million from $49.2 million for Q2 1996.</p>
</text>
